orthogonal and statement III is false. Thus original option a, index 0, is uniquely correct. This derivation agrees with the authentic worked solution and saved Correct grading; it contradicts the stored 'II only' key."}] "usage" {"q-98524" []} "basis" 2519 "retractions" [[17592186134481 :question/problem "Consider the following set of functions:\n$f_{1}(t) = \\cos t, f_{2}(t) = \\sin (2t), f_{3}(t) = t$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space $C[0, π]$ of continuous functions over $[0, π]$ is defined as\n$⟨f(t), g(t)⟩ = ∫_{0}^{π}f(t)g(t)dt$,\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $f_{1}(t)⊥f_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n2. $f_{1}(t)⊥f_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n3. $S = {f_{1}(t), f_{2}(t), f_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product"] [17592186134481 :question/answer-fields 17592186133328]] "immutable_answers" [17592186133329 17592186133330 17592186133331 17592186133332 17592186133333] "immutable_fields" [[17592186133328 :answer-field/correct] [17592186133328 :answer-field/id] [17592186133328 :answer-field/key] [17592186133328 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
